  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of three-digit even numbers, formed by the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;if the repetition of digits is not allowed, is______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "52",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>For three-digit even number, it must end with either&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>The number of three -digit even numbers ending with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p>The number of three -digit even numbers ending with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>The number of three -digit even numbers ending with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;Total three digits even numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn></math></p>",
